 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "instructions is a list of strings \"<op> <value>\" with op in plus, next, jump and value a signed decimal integer. Execution starts at index 0 with accumulator 0. plus x adds x to the accumulator and moves to the next index; next x moves to the next index (x ignored); jump x moves to index + x. Level 2: the program as given does not terminate (it repeats an instruction, or leaves the range at an index other than len). Switch exactly one instruction, jump to next or next to jump (keeping its value), so that execution reaches index len exactly without repeating an instruction. Return [switched index, accumulator at termination] for the smallest index that works, or [-1, 0] if none does.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk08-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
